<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λωπο-δύτης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>clothes-stealer</i>, esp.
			one who steals of bathers, or strips travellers, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Epigr.</u>
				4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>thief, robber, footpad,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12.44.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				206
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				497
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ra.</u>
				772
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				10.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.144
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λωποδυτῶν θάνατον αἱρεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					4.47
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἀλλοτρίων ἐπέων</span>”
				<i>plagiarist,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					11.130
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				2.19.28
			</span></i>.</div>
